cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use THALIA, please cite this software and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "THALIA: Typed Harness with Analytical Lexical-Integrated Architecture"
type: software
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Daniel Ari
    email: daniel@activeinference.institute
repository-code: "https://github.com/docxology/thalia"
url: "https://github.com/docxology/thalia/releases/tag/v0.3.1"
abstract: >-
  THALIA is an executable research harness for long-context memory systems.
  It combines typed stage contracts, inspectable context selection,
  evidence-preserving episodic state, lexical-first retrieval, and bounded
  compiler search with source-bound evaluation and reproducible artifact checks.
  The v0.3.1 patch corrects publication-manifest closure without changing
  the measured study or promoting scientific or production-readiness claims.
keywords:
  - agentic systems
  - long-context memory
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - reproducible research
  - software engineering
